{
  "comment": [
    "The cross-language reference corpus (#236, W1-A4-R1).",
    "",
    "`grammar` is the verdict all THREE parsers must reach, with the same reason",
    "token: contract.classify_reference in Python, classify_reference in",
    "oci-protocol.sh, and Get-ReferenceRejectionReason in consume.ps1. null means",
    "the grammar accepts.",
    "",
    "`canonical` is a SEPARATE authority carried only by the two parsers that",
    "consume our package: contract.parse_reference and consume.ps1's",
    "Assert-DigestReference. oci-protocol.sh deliberately does not carry it,",
    "because the local-registry controls address localhost:5000 and a shared",
    "canonical rule would manufacture a disagreement that is not one. Entries",
    "with canonical set to null are not offered to the canonical leg."
  ],
